# Experiment 1 — Without Load Balancer

| Measurement | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Average ping latency | 0.302 ms |
| HTTP response time | 6.867 ms |
| Successful requests | 1000 |
| Service available after router failure? | Clients do not complete the **ab** test. As expected because router is responsible for forwarding the clients request (No route to host (113)) |


----

Experiment 2 — With Load Balancer

| Measurement | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Average ping latency | 0.301 ms |
| Throughput (requests/sec) | 17593.10 |
| Number of active servers |  5 |
| Service available after backend failure? | Yes, when the load balancer tried to connect to the backend that was down, eventually, after a timeout, it tries another backend. |


